  "whyItCannotBeDerived": "forecast_activation_events and inventory_activation_events lived in the retail_serving schema. A from-scratch rebuild drops that schema so Alembic replays from 0001 and so a re-materialized version id is insertable, which destroys every activation event recorded before the wipe. The live stack can therefore only derive generation 1. These events are retained here, verbatim from the record committed before the wipe, so a reader can still audit the chain that was actually walked -- the same disclosure pattern as EVIDENCE_RELEASED_RUNS in tools/build_publication_selection.py."
